$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-phenylbenzamide (3b). Benzoic acid (0.61 g, 5.0 mmol), aniline (0.46
mL, 5.0 mmol) and BOP (2.65 g, 6.0 mmol) were dissolved in DCM (10 mL) to
which DIEA (2.09 ml, 12.0 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was
allowed to stirred continuously for 20 hours at room temperature. Then
additional DCM (150 mL) was added to the reaction mixture which was
washed with water (3 x 150 mL) and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 to give a
crude product, which was subjected to column purification (ethyl
acetate/n-hexane=1/4). The pure product 4b as a white solid. Yield: 0.91
g, 92%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3/DMSO-d6 =2/1) δ 9.98 (s, 1H), 7.93 - 7.86
(m, 2H), 7.71 (dd, J = 5.4, 3.3 Hz, 2H), 7.51 - 7.45 (m, 1H), 7.44 - 7.38
(m, 2H), 7.28 - 7.21 (m, 2H), 7.05 - 6.98 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 165.81, 137.87, 134.92, 131.81, 129.05, 128.74, 127.00, 124.54,
120.20. HRMS-ESI: calculated for [M+H]+ (C13H12ON): m/z 198.0919, found:
m/z 198.0906.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Strained Macrocyclic Pyridone Hexamers and Their
High Selectivity toward Cu2+ Recognition
